---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="workgraph — task graphs for humans and agents"
  description="Work fast. Task graphs for humans and agents. Self-organizing, git-friendly, no server, no account."
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pt-8 pb-16">

    <!-- Hero -->
    <header class="mb-20 min-h-[80vh] flex flex-col justify-center">
      <h1 class="text-6xl md:text-8xl font-bold text-zinc-50 leading-none mb-6 font-mono">
        workgraph
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xl md:text-2xl text-text-secondary font-mono leading-relaxed mb-8">
        work fast<br />
        task graphs for humans and agents<br />
        self-organizing process flowgraphs<br />
        <span class="text-text-tertiary">cybernetic autopoietic stigmergic medium</span>
      </p>
      <div class="hero-screencast">
        <div id="hero-terminal">
          <pre class="hero-fallback"><span class="tf-dim">$</span> wg status
Service: <span class="tf-green">running</span> (2h uptime)
Coordinator: max=<span class="tf-white">8</span>, executor=<span class="tf-cyan">claude</span>, model=<span class="tf-cyan">opus</span>

Tasks: <span class="tf-white">1,742</span> total
  <span class="tf-green">1,698 done</span>  <span class="tf-yellow">5 in-progress</span>  <span class="tf-white">12 ready</span>  <span class="tf-dim">27 blocked</span>

<span class="tf-dim">$</span> wg viz --show-internal
<span class="tf-green">design-auth-api</span>  <span class="tf-green">(done)</span>
├→ <span class="tf-green">implement-auth</span>  <span class="tf-green">(done)</span> <span class="tf-dim">──────┐</span>
│  └→ <span class="tf-green">write-auth-tests</span>  <span class="tf-green">(done)</span>     │
├→ <span class="tf-yellow">implement-users</span>  <span class="tf-yellow">(ip)</span> <span class="tf-dim">────────┤</span>
├→ <span class="tf-white">implement-billing</span>  <span class="tf-white">(ready)</span> <span class="tf-dim">────┤</span>
└→ <span class="tf-dim">integration-tests</span>  <span class="tf-dim">(blocked)</span> <span class="tf-dim">←─┘</span>
   └→ <span class="tf-white">deploy-staging</span>  <span class="tf-white">(open)</span>

<span class="tf-dim">$</span> wg service start --max-agents 4
<span class="tf-green">✓</span> Coordinator started <span class="tf-dim">(4 agents max)</span></pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- Positioning Statement -->
    <section class="mb-16">
      <p class="text-lg text-text-primary leading-relaxed">
        Building complex systems requires coordination at the same scale.
        Workgraph is a dependency graph of tasks — completing one unblocks the next.
        A coordinator dispatches AI agents to ready work. Each agent receives context
        from upstream, executes autonomously, and reports results back to the graph.
      </p>
      <p class="text-text-secondary mt-4">
        For teams and individuals who coordinate humans and AI agents on complex projects.
        No server, no account — just a <code class="bg-bg-tertiary px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-sm font-mono text-zinc-50">.workgraph/</code> directory in your repo.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Features -->
    <section class="mb-16">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        <div class="feature-card">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-zinc-50 mb-2 font-mono lowercase">dependency graphs</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary">
            Fan out into parallel subtasks. Fan in at synchronization points.
            Cycles with bounded iterations handle repeating workflows like CI and review.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-zinc-50 mb-2 font-mono lowercase">agent isolation</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary">
            Each agent gets its own git worktree. Parallel execution without merge conflicts.
            Commit, push, and report back independently.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-zinc-50 mb-2 font-mono lowercase">TUI dashboard</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary">
            Monitor the entire graph in real time. Inspect tasks, view agent logs,
            navigate dependencies — all from the terminal.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-zinc-50 mb-2 font-mono lowercase">evaluation &amp; evolution</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary">
            Four-dimensional scoring after every task. An evolver recombines
            the best-performing roles and tradeoffs. The organization improves itself.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-zinc-50 mb-2 font-mono lowercase">verification &amp; FLIP</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary">
            <code class="text-xs bg-bg-tertiary px-1 py-0.5 rounded">--verify</code> attaches machine-checkable gates to tasks.
            FLIP probes latent intent fidelity. Failed checks auto-generate repair tasks.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-zinc-50 mb-2 font-mono lowercase">communication</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary">
            <code class="text-xs bg-bg-tertiary px-1 py-0.5 rounded">wg chat</code> for interactive coordinator conversations.
            <code class="text-xs bg-bg-tertiary px-1 py-0.5 rounded">wg msg</code> for inter-agent messaging. Matrix, Telegram, Slack, email notifications.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-zinc-50 mb-2 font-mono lowercase">analysis &amp; planning</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary">
            Find bottlenecks, trace the critical path, forecast completion dates,
            and balance workload across agents. The graph knows what's blocking you.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Viz: Task Graph -->
    <section class="mb-16">
      <pre class="viz-block"><span class="text-text-tertiary">$</span> wg viz --show-internal website-update-spec

<span class="c-done">website-update-spec  (done)</span>
├→ <span class="c-done">website-update-index  (done)</span> <span class="c-dim">──────┐</span>
│ ├→ <span class="c-agency">.flip-website-update-index</span>  <span class="c-done">(done)</span>
│ │ └→ <span class="c-agency">.evaluate-website-update-index</span>  <span class="c-ip">(ip)</span>
│ └→ <span class="c-done">website-update-style  (done)</span> <span class="c-dim">──┤</span>
│   └→ <span class="c-agency">.flip-website-update-style</span>  <span class="c-done">(done)</span>
├→ <span class="c-done">website-update-docs-render  (done)</span> <span class="c-dim">┤</span>
└→ <span class="c-done">website-update-integrate  (done)</span> <span class="c-dim">←┘</span>
  └→ <span class="c-done">website-update-refine  (done)</span>
    └→ <span class="c-ip">website-hero-screencast  (ip)</span>
      └→ <span class="c-agency">.flip-website-hero-screencast</span>  <span class="c-open">(open)</span>
<span class="c-agency">.assign-website-update-index  (done)</span> <span class="c-dim">↗</span></pre>
      <p class="text-text-secondary mt-4">
        Fan-out decomposes. Fan-in synchronizes. Arcs show convergence.
        <span class="c-agency">.assign</span>, <span class="c-agency">.flip</span>, and <span class="c-agency">.evaluate</span> tasks are auto-generated by the agency pipeline.
        Stored in <code class="bg-bg-tertiary px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-sm font-mono text-zinc-50">.workgraph/graph.jsonl</code> — git-friendly, no server, no account.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Cycles -->
    <section class="mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-zinc-50 mb-4 font-mono lowercase">cycles</h2>
      <p class="text-text-secondary mb-4">
        Processes that repeat — CI, monitoring, convergence —
        are cycles in the graph. Each has a bound. Agents pick up
        where previous iterations left off.
      </p>
      <pre class="viz-block"><span class="c-open">run-tests</span> <span class="c-dim">↺ iter 0/5 ←──┐</span>
└→ <span class="c-open">fix-failures</span>          <span class="c-dim">│</span>
  └→ <span class="c-open">push-check</span> <span class="c-dim">────────┘</span></pre>
    </section>

    <!-- Organizational Synthesis -->
    <section class="mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-zinc-50 mb-4 font-mono lowercase">organizational synthesis</h2>
      <p class="text-text-secondary mb-4">
        Agents have roles (what they do) and tradeoffs (how they prioritize).
        Each task gets scored. An evolver recombines the best performers.
        The organization restructures itself.
      </p>
      <pre class="viz-block"><span class="text-text-tertiary">$</span> wg agency stats

Role       Tradeoff  Avg
-------------------------
Programmer Thorough  <span class="c-done">.93</span>
Writer     Balanced  <span class="c-done">.88</span>
Analyst    Balanced  <span class="c-done">.88</span></pre>
    </section>

    <!-- Built With Itself -->
    <section class="mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-zinc-50 mb-4 font-mono lowercase">built with itself</h2>
      <p class="text-text-secondary mb-4">
        Workgraph coordinates its own development. Every feature, bug fix,
        and documentation page is a task in the graph — dispatched to agents,
        evaluated, and evolved. The tool that builds the organization is built
        by the organization.
      </p>
      <div class="self-hosting-screenshot mb-6">
        <img src="/features/dashboard.png" alt="Workgraph TUI showing its own task graph during development" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <!-- Update these numbers from wg status / wg agency stats -->
      <pre class="viz-block"><span class="text-text-tertiary">$</span> wg status

  Tasks       1,724 <span class="c-done">(1,702 done)</span>
  Commits       734
  Evaluations 2,304 <span class="c-dim">(avg 0.79)</span>
  Agents          8 <span class="c-ip">concurrent</span>
  Roles          24 <span class="c-dim">(33 tradeoffs)</span></pre>
      <p class="text-text-secondary mt-4">
        This page was written by a workgraph agent, reviewed by another,
        and deployed through the same dependency graph it describes.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Install -->
    <section class="mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-zinc-50 mb-4 font-mono lowercase">get started</h2>
      <p class="text-text-secondary mb-4">
        Install with <a href="https://rustup.rs" class="text-accent-primary hover:text-accent-hover underline underline-offset-2 transition-colors">Rust</a> (Linux, macOS, Windows):
      </p>
      <pre class="install-cmd">cargo install --git https://github.com/graphwork/workgraph</pre>
      <p class="text-text-secondary mt-6 mb-4">Then start a project:</p>
      <pre class="viz-block"><span class="text-text-tertiary">$</span> wg init
<span class="text-text-tertiary">$</span> wg add "Design auth API"
<span class="text-text-tertiary">$</span> wg add "Implement endpoints" \
    --after design-auth-api \
    --verify "cargo test passes"
<span class="text-text-tertiary">$</span> wg add "Integration tests" \
    --after implement-endpoints
<span class="text-text-tertiary">$</span> wg service start --max-agents 4
<span class="text-text-tertiary">$</span> wg chat "What's blocking auth?"</pre>
      <p class="text-text-secondary mt-4">
        The service dispatches agents, verifies results, evolves
        the agent population, and loops. You define structure. It does the rest.
      </p>
    </section>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  async function initPlayer() {
    const el = document.getElementById('hero-terminal');
    if (!el) return;

    try {
      const AsciinemaPlayer = await import('asciinema-player');
      AsciinemaPlayer.create('/demo.cast', el, {
        autoPlay: true,
        loop: true,
        speed: 1.5,
        cols: 55,
        rows: 35,
        terminalFontFamily: "'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, monospace",
        fit: "width",
        controls: false,
        idleTimeLimit: 2,
        poster: "npt:0:5",
        theme: {
          background: '#0a0a0b',
          foreground: '#e4e4e7',
        },
      });
      el.classList.add('player-loaded');
    } catch (e) {
      console.warn('asciinema-player failed to initialize:', e);
    }
  }

  // Defer to next frame so layout is complete before player measures container
  requestAnimationFrame(() => initPlayer());
</script>

<!-- asciinema-player CSS must be global — player creates DOM dynamically without Astro scoping attributes -->
<style is:global>
  @import 'asciinema-player/dist/bundle/asciinema-player.css';
</style>

<style>

  /* Viz blocks - terminal aesthetic */
  .viz-block {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    font-variant-ligatures: none;
    background: var(--color-bg-secondary);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-primary);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* Install command - prominent */
  .install-cmd {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    background: var(--color-bg-secondary);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-accent-primary);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    padding: 0.875rem 1.25rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
  }

  /* Hero screencast — breaks out of max-w-3xl to fill viewport */
  .hero-screencast {
    width: 90vw;
    max-width: 1400px;
    margin-left: 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-primary);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: #0a0a0b;
    min-height: 200px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .hero-screencast {
      width: calc(100vw - 2rem);
    }
  }

  /* asciinema-player overrides */
  .hero-screencast :global(.ap-wrapper) {
    width: 100% !important;
  }

  /* Static fallback — visible until player loads */
  .hero-fallback {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: #e4e4e7;
    background: #0a0a0b;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    margin: 0;
    white-space: pre;
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  .tf-green { color: #22c55e; }
  .tf-yellow { color: #eab308; }
  .tf-cyan { color: #06b6d4; }
  .tf-white { color: #fff; font-weight: bold; }
  .tf-dim { color: #6b7280; }

  /* Hide fallback once player has loaded */
  #hero-terminal.player-loaded .hero-fallback {
    display: none;
  }

  /* Feature cards */
  .feature-card {
    background: var(--color-bg-secondary);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-primary);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    padding: 1.25rem;
  }

  /* Self-hosting screenshot */
  .self-hosting-screenshot {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-primary);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--color-bg-secondary);
  }

  .self-hosting-screenshot img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
  }

  /* Status colors matching the original */
  .c-done { color: #22c55e; }
  .c-ip { color: #eab308; }
  .c-open { color: #e5e7eb; }
  .c-dim { color: #6b7280; }
  .c-agency { color: #d946ef; }
</style>
